caption: Practicum
tradition-component: practicum

Track FP actually spent on activation separately for each Jutsu the practitioner uses. Every full 12 FP spent activating one source Jutsu produces 1 learning hour that may be assigned to one Jutsu for which that source Jutsu is a direct or indirect prerequisite. This benefit applies to Jutsu from any Jutsu Tradition the character can legally access, not only Shadow Arts. The target Jutsu must already be legally accessible to the character through Class access or actual instruction, and all ordinary prerequisite, Potence, tree, and purchase requirements still apply. Practicum learning hours stack with ordinary study and use the Kung Fu Accelerated Training rules normally, including Training Experience accounting. Practicum is not an Experience Loop or Enhancement award and generates no character points except through ordinary Improvement Through Study. A single Jutsu activation's FP expenditure may generate learning hours through only one Jutsu-use training engine. If the same expenditure would qualify for Practicum and another such engine, including Matukai Tempering, choose which engine receives it; the same FP may not be counted twice.
